---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Card from '../../../components/Card.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { withBase } from '../../../lib/url';
import { byInsertionDesc } from '../../../lib/insertionOrder';

const leggende = (await getCollection('leggendeEn')).sort(byInsertionDesc);
---

<Layout title="Legends" description="Legends and folk tales handed down in San Vito Romano.">
  <h1>Legends</h1>
  <p class="meta">Stories, mysteries and folk tales passed down from generation to generation.</p>

  <p>
    Every town has a written history and a told one. The second is not found in books: it lives in
    grandparents' voices, in evenings by the fireplace, in the names given to an alley, a fountain,
    a boulder by the road. The legends of San Vito Romano are made this way: witches who turn into
    cats at night, creatures that play tricks on those fetching water, brigands, lucky simpletons
    and figures that seem to have stepped out of a fairy tale.
  </p>
  <p>
    It does not matter how much of it is true. Their beauty lies in the way a whole community has
    been able to look at its own places with wonder, and in the thread that still ties those who
    listen to those who used to tell them. Reading them is a way to know the town from the inside,
    and to keep passing them on.
  </p>

  <div class="card-grid">
    {
      leggende.map((l) => (
        <Card
          href={withBase(`en/leggende/${l.id}/`)}
          title={l.data.title}
          description={l.data.description}
          image={l.data.immagine}
        />
      ))
    }
  </div>
</Layout>
